The packaging pipeline preserves the project license, runtime npm dependency
licenses, Electron's MIT license and the exact target Electron distribution's
LICENSES.chromium.html bytes. The app displays these documents as plain text
in Settings > Open source licenses. Packaged resources/licenses/index.json
records document sizes and SHA256 hashes. resources/licenses/sbom.cdx.json
contains the runtime component inventory; Electron's bundled third-party
components and their full terms are recorded in electron-third-party.txt.

Development artifacts include a source revision, package-lock hash, SHA256SUMS,
build-report.json and a corresponding-source archive. Ad-hoc/unsigned build
verification is not publisher signing or notarization. Public release readiness
is tracked separately in docs/developer/guides/release-readiness.md.

Windows portable launchers use NSIS3.12 (toolset1.2.1) with built-in zlib
compression. StdUtils1.14 remains an unmodified LGPL-2.1-or-later plug-in;
its author clarification, bundled notices and complete corresponding source
are provided in resources/licenses and resources/third-party-source.
The reviewed DLL SHA256 is recorded in the component inventory.
